  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1985-p19.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The new perimeter is \\(2(1.1\\ell + 1.1w) = 1.1 \\cdot 2(\\ell + w),\\) which is \\(1.1\\) times the old perimeter.\n\nThat is a \\(10\\%\\) increase.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "The perimeter is \\(2(\\ell + w)\\)",
        "Multiplying both \\(\\ell\\) and \\(w\\) by \\(1.1\\) multiplies the whole perimeter by \\(1.1\\)"
      ],
